      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A diesel turbocharger works by harnessing the energy of hot, outgoing exhaust gases to spin a turbine, which is connected by a shaft to a compressor. The compressor then sucks in ambient air and forces it into the engine's intake manifold at a much higher pressure than normal. This forced induction, or \"boost,\" allows the engine to burn more fuel efficiently, leading to more power. Think of it like a tiny, high-speed windmill powered by your engine's waste gas.",
