    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. what about the sound though? i've noticed turbochargers make this really specific high pitched whistling or whining noise when they're spooling up. is there something mechanical about the design that causes that sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The whistling or whining sound you hear when a turbo spools up is primarily due to the high-velocity airflow rushing through the compressor housing. When the turbine spins up rapidly, it forces a massive volume of air through the compressor wheel and the intricate passages of the housing. This rapid movement of air, much like a high-speed stream of water through a narrow pipe, creates aerodynamic noise. It's essentially the sound of very fast air being forced through designed pathways.",
      "source": "target",
